# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Node / frontend ---
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# --- Environment / secrets ---
.env
!.env.example

# --- ML model checkpoints (large binaries, not source) ---
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.pkl

# --- Local application storage (uploaded/generated images) ---
backend/storage/

# --- Local Claude Code tooling config (machine-specific) ---
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Dataset-extraction pipeline generated output ---
# The pipeline's source code and its small checked-in datasets/**/raw/ sample
# fixtures stay tracked. Everything below is where it writes generated data
# once actually run (currently empty per project_manifest.json) and must not
# be committed once it is.
**/logs/
**/output/
**/datasets/merged/
**/datasets/normalized/
**/datasets/versions/
**/datasets/assets/
**/datasets/quarantine/
**/datasets/master/
**/datasets/processed/
**/datasets/*/processed/
**/datasets/*/quarantine/
**/datasets/*/versions/
**/datasets/*/reports/
**/datasets/*/metadata/
**/datasets/quality/

# Real acquired source data (hundreds of MB; downloaded/derived by the scripts
# in _ingestion_tools/, never hand-authored). The original 4-row sample_*.csv
# fixtures alongside them stay tracked; brand_facts.csv (60 rows, the verified
# Wikipedia/Wikidata output) is small enough to track as a record of what the
# fetch actually returned.
**/datasets/raw/zappos/
**/datasets/raw/amazon/
**/datasets/reviews/raw/amazon_reviews.jsonl
**/datasets/market/raw/amazon_market.csv
**/datasets/product_intelligence/raw/product_intelligence.csv
**/_ingestion_tools/*.log
**/_ingestion_tools/__pycache__/

# --- OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
